WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.930
The replay interface starts with the
same Monday eight o’clock request.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.170
It first resolves consistent
calendar metadata,

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.310
then sends a target free
request to prediction.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:16.890
The response contains the estimate, simple
baseline, support and model identities.

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:20.370
It contains no observed count or residual.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.810
A separate show outcome action retrieves
a historical observation for comparison.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.410
The server holds that
separate record for replay,

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.770
while the predictor can run without it.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:37.080
Browser checks confirm the client makes
no observation request before the explicit

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:37.990
action.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:42.640
This gives the information boundary
visible behavior instead of leaving it

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:43.710
only in a comment.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:51.010
This screenshot shows the completed
comparison after the outcome action.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:55.860
The forecast card displays three hundred
and forty nine point five rentals per

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:56.430
hour.

00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:00.220
The global training mean is one
hundred and forty three point eight,

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:04.310
and the fitted group has two hundred
and forty eight supporting hours.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.600
The separate outcome card displays four
hundred and twenty with signed error

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.610
negative seventy point five zero.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.500
The interface rounds for reading,

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:18.450
while the API retains the
full floating point values.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:20.070
Issue time,

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:20.780
schema,

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:21.910
used fields

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:26.660
and model and bundle hashes remain
inspectable so the estimate has an

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:28.050
identifiable contract.

00:01:30.232 --> 00:01:35.422
The adapter obtains a consistent request
and sends it through the saved predictor.

00:01:36.132 --> 00:01:38.502
Prediction reuses fitted state,

00:01:38.892 --> 00:01:42.482
and no button click or server
startup fits another model.

00:01:43.032 --> 00:01:48.212
The separate observation lookup validates
the same historical date boundary and can

00:01:48.212 --> 00:01:49.402
return unavailable.

00:01:50.172 --> 00:01:54.952
Application data is checked against the
predictor and dataset identities before

00:01:54.952 --> 00:01:55.822
serving.

00:01:56.372 --> 00:01:59.362
Preparation is an
explicit earlier command,

00:01:59.572 --> 00:02:02.482
separate from loading and
serving the saved state.

00:02:03.132 --> 00:02:08.692
The HTTP server binds to loopback
and serves fixed packaged assets and

00:02:08.692 --> 00:02:09.162
routes.

00:02:09.672 --> 00:02:14.482
It does not turn a browser supplied string
into a file path or training command.

00:02:16.608 --> 00:02:19.858
Change to January second
at three in the morning,

00:02:20.088 --> 00:02:22.818
a genuinely unrecorded validation hour.

00:02:23.508 --> 00:02:27.758
The recorded date metadata still
supplies a valid calendar request.

00:02:28.368 --> 00:02:31.818
The model can therefore produce
an estimate from its fitted group.

00:02:32.288 --> 00:02:36.238
The observation lookup returns
unavailable with no target,

00:02:36.748 --> 00:02:40.078
and the interface says an actual
count and error are absent.

00:02:40.848 --> 00:02:45.468
It does not treat the missing count as
zero rentals or add a row to the benchmark

00:02:45.468 --> 00:02:46.538
denominator.

00:02:47.148 --> 00:02:51.198
An available estimate and unavailable
observed evidence can coexist.

00:02:51.908 --> 00:02:56.488
Handling both explicitly keeps the
replay faithful to the source rather than

00:02:56.488 --> 00:02:58.938
manufacturing a complete calendar grid.

00:03:00.983 --> 00:03:04.233
Now change to a future
twenty thirteen date.

00:03:04.723 --> 00:03:07.353
That is outside the
historical validation domain,

00:03:07.543 --> 00:03:09.593
even though its hour could be encoded.

00:03:10.183 --> 00:03:11.763
The backend rejects it,

00:03:11.763 --> 00:03:16.003
and the browser clears the old forecast
instead of leaving three hundred and forty

00:03:16.003 --> 00:03:18.793
nine point five looking
like the new answer.

00:03:19.423 --> 00:03:22.613
Reserved test dates,
non hourly timestamps,

00:03:22.923 --> 00:03:26.953
unknown schema and a request
containing an outcome also fail.

00:03:27.503 --> 00:03:30.553
These errors differ from a
valid missing observation.

00:03:31.223 --> 00:03:34.843
The working application preserves
the earlier information and support

00:03:34.843 --> 00:03:35.553
boundaries,

00:03:35.843 --> 00:03:40.363
while the explicit message helps the
user understand why no forecast is being

00:03:40.363 --> 00:03:40.993
displayed.

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:48.460
Actual browser checks exercise quiet
Monday, Sunday and June requests,

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:53.000
the observed comparison,
missing evidence and rejected dates.

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:58.823
The layout passes at four widths from
fourteen hundred and forty to three

00:03:58.823 --> 00:04:03.280
hundred and twenty pixels without
document overflow or JavaScript errors.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:08.080
An isolated installed wheel
serves its packaged HTML,

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:09.960
JavaScript and CSS

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:13.520
while an audit hook denies
all source project access.

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:18.610
The user can run the application from
saved assets rather than an active

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:19.600
training notebook.

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:21.960
That is implemented local behavior.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:24.380
It does not establish hosted recovery,

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:25.920
operational usefulness

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:28.100
or a final held out assessment.

